ames>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>CD4&#x0002b;CD25&#x0002b; T-cell populations expressing CD134 and GITR are associated with disease activity in patients with Wegener's granulomatosis.</article-title><source>Nephrol Dial Transplant</source></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005287-Hermiston1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hermiston</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Xu</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Weiss</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>CD45: a critical regulator of signaling thresholds in immune cells.</article-title><source>Annu Rev Immunol</source><volume>21</volume><fpage>107</fpage><lpage>137</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12414720</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005287-Streuli1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Streuli</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hall</surname><given-names>LR</given-names></name><name><surname>Saga</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Schlossman</surname><given-names>SF</given-names></name><name><surname>Saito</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><year>1987</year><article-title>Differential usage of three exons generates at least five different mRNAs encoding human leukocyte common antigens.</article-title><source>J Exp Med</source><volume>166</volume><fpage>1548</fpage><lpage>1566</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2824653</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005287-Tchilian1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tchilian</surname><given-names>EZ</given-names></name><name><surname>Beverley</surname><given-names>PC</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Altere